  qa:issue "The sprint lists REQ-RT-0005 and explicitly owns lock/socket cleanup and worker startup after the successful stores callback, but omits active REQ-RT-0002, which governs the singleton daemon.lock lifecycle and stores-callback ordering. The requirement is directly touched by WI9 and cannot be inferred as out of scope." ;
  qa:recommendation "Add REQ-RT-0002 to the sprint requirements list and retain evidence that the runtime takes daemon.lock before the stores callback and holds it through run/shutdown." .
